WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.238
You ask Iris to run a task once.

00:00:03.238 --> 00:00:05.634
The connection closes before the reply arrives.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:07.687
Can you safely send it again?

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:10.566
Start with the practice case.

00:00:10.846 --> 00:00:12.793
Check the original attempt.

00:00:13.073 --> 00:00:15.339
Then open its saved receipt.

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:20.397
Here, one dispatch was recorded, and no automatic retry occurred.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.847
Next, compare the receipt with fresh task history.

00:00:25.127 --> 00:00:27.685
A missing reply leaves a question.

00:00:27.965 --> 00:00:33.024
The saved record and the later observation give you something
concrete to check.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.756
The practice agent corrects its earlier answer after checking the
evidence.

00:00:39.036 --> 00:00:41.413
You can see why its judgment changed.

00:00:41.693 --> 00:00:43.939
Keep the receipt and continue.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.990
This update brings the question, the evidence, and your next
decision into one readable case.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:52.587
Start with the result.

00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:55.782
Open the supporting records whenever you need them.

00:00:56.833 --> 00:00:59.996
The case now leads with a plain-language report.

00:00:59.996 --> 00:01:04.739
Three stages organize the current task, what happened, and the
supporting detail.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:09.087
The practice walkthrough makes that path usable on a first visit.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:15.566
Here, an agent is a language model assigned a job and a limited set
of tools.

00:01:15.846 --> 00:01:19.458
Battery's reviewer checks a claim against the evidence.

00:01:19.738 --> 00:01:25.443
Its investigator chooses a permitted follow-up, such as reading an
operation receipt.

00:01:25.723 --> 00:01:28.872
Their answers and evidence stay with the case.

00:01:28.872 --> 00:01:31.627
You decide whether another operation should run.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.055
Here is a retained native run on real Iris.

00:01:36.335 --> 00:01:39.944
The small reviewer wrongly marked the outcome as failed.

00:01:40.224 --> 00:01:43.751
A larger investigator selected a receipt check.

00:01:44.031 --> 00:01:47.323
The evidence supported a later passing review.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:56.646
Battery keeps two judgments separate: whether the rule's assertion
is supported, and whether the observed result meets the check.

00:01:56.646 --> 00:02:00.119
A persuasive explanation cannot supply a missing receipt.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.221
In the interface, source links open the record behind a claim.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:11.393
The technical view retains earlier answers, evidence reads, and the
recorded conclusion.

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:15.014
You can inspect the details without losing the case.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:18.162
Now consider a different case.

00:02:18.162 --> 00:02:22.770
The original receipt passed, but a later read shows different settings.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:25.703
Battery asks whether that change was intentional.

00:02:25.703 --> 00:02:28.636
Historical success does not answer that question.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:37.134
An optional full-case review brings the saved receipt, review history,
current settings, and human choice together.

00:02:37.414 --> 00:02:43.872
Its interpretation stays separate from the recorded result and the
controls that authorize changes.

00:02:44.933 --> 00:02:47.378
Here, choose to keep the current settings.

00:02:47.658 --> 00:02:50.546
Write the reason, then record the decision.

00:02:50.826 --> 00:02:54.868
Recording that intention does not change the configuration.

00:02:55.148 --> 00:02:59.775
A new operation still needs its own preparation and authorization.

00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:03.357
The same case works on a phone.

00:03:03.357 --> 00:03:07.323
Swipe between stages, open a source, and return to the question.

00:03:07.323 --> 00:03:10.567
The interface keeps the evidence close to the decision.

00:03:11.633 --> 00:03:17.942
A separate connected test recovered a real Iris configuration receipt
after a lost reply.

00:03:17.942 --> 00:03:21.096
Reusing the execution key returned that receipt.

00:03:21.096 --> 00:03:26.053
The published report includes the first wrong review and its
correction.

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:30.019
The browser walkthrough uses simulated records.

00:03:30.019 --> 00:03:34.828
The native workflow runs inside Iris with configured model access.

00:03:34.828 --> 00:03:43.003
These checks cover specific operations and failure cases; they do
not establish that every downstream service works.

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:48.966
Try the practice case, then inspect the source and the native setup.

00:03:48.966 --> 00:03:53.865
Armada Battery keeps the attempt, the evidence, and the person's
decision connected.
